<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schöllenen Gorge</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Schöllenen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Schöllenen Gorge is a narrow gorge of the Reuss River in the canton of Uri, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, between Göschenen and Andermatt on the route to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotthard-pass">Gotthard Pass</a>. The building of a bridge through it in the early thirteenth century, later called the Devil's Bridge, opened the Gotthard route. In 1799 Russian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-suvorov">Suvorov</a> fought the French there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schollenen-gorge.jpg" alt="Schöllenen Gorge" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Barcelona)_The_devil%27s_Bridge_and_Sch%C3%B6llen_Gorge_1802_-_William_Turner_-_Tate_Britain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
